        "node_id": "n_3_40ff72",
        "thought_text": "Revised Thought-1: Instead of using BFS to calculate distances, use cycle detection within the graph to determine the minimum number of swaps required. Each cycle of length k requires (k-1) swaps to sort. Iterate through the permutation and identify cycles, summing up the necessary swaps for each cycle. This approach ensures that we efficiently find the minimum number of swaps without unnecessary computations.",
