        "thought_text": "Thought-2: Instead of creating a graph where each node represents a permutation, use a more efficient approach by directly applying the allowed swaps to the current permutation and keeping track of the number of swaps made. This way, you avoid the overhead of constructing and traversing a large graph, focusing instead on finding the shortest sequence of valid swaps to reach the sorted permutation.",
