        "thought_text": "Thought-2: Recognize that the problem can be reduced to finding the number of cycles in the permutation graph where each node represents an element and edges represent allowed swaps. Each cycle of length \\( k \\) requires \\( k-1 \\) swaps to sort. By identifying all cycles and summing up the necessary swaps for each, we can determine the minimum number of swaps required. This approach leverages cycle detection to efficiently solve the problem without unnecessary computations.",
